Package: modem-guard
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: modemmanager,
         network-manager,
         raspi-utils,
         iputils-ping,
         systemd
Recommends: gpiod
Maintainer: modem-guard contributors <techbasegit@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/@REPO@
Description: Keeps a GSM modem connected, with soft and hard reset recovery
 Connects a GSM modem at boot using a configured APN and keeps the link up,
 recovering a wedged modem by escalating from a ModemManager soft reset to a
 GPIO power cycle.
 .
 The work is done by ModemManager, NetworkManager and pinctrl; this package
 adds only the decision logic that determines when a reset is warranted, plus
 the systemd units that carry the resets out.
 .
 A hung bearer - the modem reporting "connected" while no traffic passes - is
 detected by a ping bound to the modem's own interface, so a working Ethernet
 uplink cannot mask a dead modem.
 .
 This package is an example of how to combine existing open-source components.
 It is not a product and carries no warranty.
